## 3. QR Code Scanning & Verification Mechanism

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Customer as Receiver Customer
    participant App as RIDO App / SMS Engine
    actor Verifier as Carrier (Door-to-Door) OR Hub Official (NURTW)
    participant Auth as Fastify API Server
    participant Escrow as Escrow Engine

    App-->>Customer: Generates Unique Pickup ID (e.g. RIDO-8F92) + HMAC QR Payload
    Customer->>Verifier: Presents QR Code / Unique Pickup ID on arrival
    Verifier->>Auth: POST /deliveries/:id/verify-qr (qr_payload or pickup_id)
    Auth->>Auth: Decrypt HMAC & Validate Delivery Match
    Auth->>Escrow: Release Escrow Funds to Carrier / Hub
    Auth-->>Verifier: 200 OK — Delivery Confirmed & Package Handed Over
    Auth-->>Customer: SMS Notification: "Package Successfully Received"
```

### QR Payload Security Composition
- **HMAC Signatures**: QR code contains an encrypted token `HMAC-SHA256(delivery_id + receiver_id + timestamp, JWT_SECRET)`.
- **Offline / Manual Fallback**: If QR scanning fails or camera is unavailable, the 6-digit **Unique Pickup ID** + Receiver Phone OTP serves as manual fallback.

---

## 4. Authentication & Session Management Architecture

- **Auth Pattern**: Passwordless Phone/Email OTP verification.
- **Tokens**: Short-lived 15m Access JWT + 7-day Refresh Token.
- **WebSocket Security**: Handshake JWT validation scoped to `delivery_id`.

---

## 5. Non-Discriminatory Proximity Dispatch & Real-Time Map Tracking

1. **PostGIS Proximity Search**: Searches online carriers (individual or fleet drivers) within 5km–15km radius.
2. **Accept/Decline Cascade**: 30-second timer per carrier.
3. **Live GPS Stream**: Broadcasts live map pings via WebSockets to Senders, Receivers, and Fleet Admins simultaneously.

